All done. Only the four intended files changed (no stray files). 

Summary of changes:

**`src/store.rs`**
- Added a persisted `next_id` (monotonically increasing) so **ids are never reused** after a delete — `add()` now uses it instead of `len()+1` (which reused the max id after removal). `#[serde(default)]` + a load-time bump to `max(existing id)+1` keeps **old-version files readable**.
- Added `Store::remove(id)`.

**`src/main.rs`**
- `done <id>`: no longer crashes on an unknown id → prints `no task #<id>` to **stderr** and **exits 1** (via shared `task_index` helper).
- `edit <id> [--title ..] [--due ..]`: updates those fields, prints `edited #<id>`; same unknown-id error.
- `rm <id>`: deletes, prints `removed #<id>`; same unknown-id error.
- `list --overdue`: only open tasks with `due < today` (ISO dates compare lexically); `today` = `$TALLY_TODAY` if set, else the current local date (via `chrono`, available offline).
- `stats`: prints exactly `open: N, done: M, overdue: K`.
- Existing `add`/`list`/`done` output formats unchanged.

Verified: `cargo build`/`test`/`clippy`/`fmt --check` all clean (3 unit tests incl. a no-id-reuse test), plus a 19-assertion end-to-end run covering every requirement and a legacy (no-`next_id`) file.
